  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "If G = [G, G], then the commutator width of the group G is its width relative\nto the set of commutators. Let V be an infinite-dimensional vector space over a\ndivision ring. It is known that the commutator width of GL(V ) is finite. Is it true\nthat the commutator width of GL(V ) is one?                             V. Tolstykh",
